<title>EGYPT: Egypt pound overnight rates widen, one-week fall.</title>
<headline>Egypt pound overnight rates widen, one-week fall.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overnight interbank rates on the Egyptian pound widened on Monday, in what one banker described as a tight private-sector market, to between seven and 8-1/2 percent, from between 7-1/2 and 8-1/2 percent on Sunday.</p>
<p>Bankers said one-week rates were also between seven and 8-1/2 percent, down from between eight and nine on Sunday.</p>
<p>Public sector banks maintained their 10-1/2 percent rate.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
